# Gearbox shift timer and rpm ramps, DUSA's at 30 Hz (CCE auto 0604D83C,
# manual 0604D94C; DUSA 0602F17C / 0602F270).
#
# Shift timer (CCE +0xB8, DUSA +0xD8): set to +N on an upshift, -N on a
# downshift, counts to 0 one per tick. DUSA N = 5, CCE N = 16. While it is
# negative (manual) the rpm is held at an overshoot that falls each tick, and
# the rev-limit check (rpm >= 8500 -> brake 255) can't fire. The rev-limit brake starts N + 1 ticks after a
# downshift: DUSA 6 x 3 = 18 frames, so 30 Hz N = 8 (9 x 2 = 18 frames).
# Downshift overshoot: DUSA +1250 falling 250 per tick over 5 ticks; CCE
# +4000 falling 250 over 16. 30 Hz: +1250 falling 1250 / 8 = 156 per tick.
# Engine-rpm follow (CCE +0xD4, DUSA +0xE4): per-gear step limits per tick,
# not rescaled in CCE; increments x 2/3.
